Translate this Unity C# character controller movement into Unreal Engine 5.7 C++ with coordinate system adaptation:
```csharp
Vector3 move = transform.forward * input.y + transform.right * input.x;
controller.Move(move * speed * Time.deltaTime);
```

In Unity, space is Left-Handed, Y-Up (meters). In Unreal Engine 5.7, space is Left-Handed, Z-Up (centimeters). 1m = 100cm.

Unreal C++ translation:
```cpp
FVector Forward = GetActorForwardVector();
FVector Right = GetActorRightVector();
FVector MoveDirection = (Forward * InputY + Right * InputX).GetSafeNormal();
AddMovementInput(MoveDirection, Speed * 100.0f * DeltaSeconds);
```
Key differences: Unity `controller.Move` integrates delta time manually in meters; Unreal `AddMovementInput` handles sub-stepping through `UCharacterMovementComponent` with velocity in cm/s.

